/** @page user-guide User guide

@section building Building

atpg needs a C++20 compiler and CMake 3.21 or newer. slang, Catch2, CLI11 and
fmt are fetched automatically on first configure, so a network connection is
needed then.

OR-Tools 9.15 or newer and pkg-config are required system packages, resolved
with `find_package` rather than fetched, because building OR-Tools from source
is far slower than every other dependency:

```sh
brew install or-tools pkg-config   # macOS
cmake -B build
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build
```

@section invocation Invocation

```sh
atpg <file.sv> --top <module> [options]
```

The design must be built from SystemVerilog gate primitives (`and`, `nand`,
`or`, `nor`, `xor`, `xnor`, `buf`, `not`) and must be purely combinational.

@section options Options

- `--dump-graph <path>` writes the flattened gate graph as Graphviz dot.
- `--dump-faults <path>` writes the collapsed fault list, one line per class.
- `--generate-tests <path>` writes a pattern, or `redundant`/`aborted`, per
  fault class.
- `--drop` makes `--generate-tests` use the generate-and-drop loop, which
  fault-simulates each pattern so faults it already covers never reach the
  solver.
- `--time-limit <seconds>` bounds the per-fault CP-SAT solve.
- `--stimulus <path>` reads newline-separated `0`/`1` vectors and prints the
  simulated outputs.
- `--fault-sim <path>` fault-simulates the `--stimulus` vectors and writes a
  coverage report. This deliberately reads the stimulus specifically, rather
  than the run's current pattern set: it measures an externally supplied vector
  set.
- `--compact <path>` compacts the run's pattern set and writes it in the format
  `--stimulus` reads.
- `--stil <path>` writes the run's pattern set as an IEEE 1450 STIL program.

@section pattern-set The run's pattern set

`--compact` and `--stil` both consume whatever the latest stage produced: the
compacted set if `--compact` ran, otherwise the generated set if
`--generate-tests` ran, otherwise the `--stimulus` set. So a full run is a
single invocation:

```sh
atpg design.sv --top top --generate-tests tests.txt --compact compact.txt \
    --stil design.stil
```

@section stil-caveat A caveat on the STIL output

The emitted STIL follows the IEEE 1450-1999 structure, but has not been
validated against a real STIL reader. The tests check the program's semantics -
signal order, group membership, stimulus values and expected responses - not
that a tester would load it.

*/
